+# Sparse heatmap result
+
+**8/8 local heatmap workflows and 8/8 unchanged native31 workflows pass.** All observations are synthetic: **0/1344 real triplets compared**, `fullAcceptance=false`.
+
+The old dense mapper's genuine RED wrote 18 children for 6 triplets and inferred 3-column grids. The corrected source contract writes exactly 6 children for the six observed triplets across 3 maps, with the declared 16x12 grid, source ordinal, exact x/y/action counts and observed zeros. No unobserved zero or second acting_ltr/home_ltr rotation is introduced. Source actions totals remain independent exact observations, including explicit null.
+
+Absent/null/empty cells remain distinct parent states; outer teams/players collections have separate coverage states/counts. 74 invalid families and 6 identity/cohort conflicts refuse atomically. The additional ambiguous playerRef-in-teams RED is retained. A variant and changed synthetic source observation preserve the old snapshot and create distinct complete parent versions. A fresh exec process reuses both core and family receipts with 94 tables/67 sequences unchanged: `9f8ce42c5152e6d6b6ce135f50caf8f3be0c46b445b0bf243ee88d5360b1a2a7`.
+
+The current source lookup/native31 VERSION and mapping semantics were not changed. The exact unchanged native31 test/spec was executed via the checked-in evidence-redirection entry point; only output DOC moved here. Its own 8/8 receipt is `native31-regression/runs/20261104T222225118985Z-heatmap-regression/result.json`. Protected native31/pilot proofs/tests/ledgers, model and sealed 012/013 are byte-identical to 5745197060; no 014, frontend/CI/WORKLOG or source-service/commit action occurred in this lot.
+
+Profile evaluation uses actual SQL: exact synthetic name/shirt '09' is stored in existing observed-profile columns and joins uniquely by actor/source/source_record/variant/context/selected cohort. The repeated-team observation from another collection collides with the existing actor/context/variant key. This proves a conditional candidate, not a general mapping or a need for DDL. Names/shirts remain qualified gaps in the spatial importer; no value is hidden in diagnostic JSON, and no global profile/played/tenure is inferred.
+
+Other limits: absent actions has no exact state column and is refused; explicit null is accepted. Existing map rows need declared valid grid/metres/frame, even if cells is absent/null/empty. Incompatible double precision or unknown frames reject; dimensions/units are never guessed from list shape. The first correction-fixture failure is kept: the SQL no-op guard stopped reuse of the old source record and was not weakened.
+
+Final receipt: `runs/20261104T222221141055Z-sparse-final-bounded-contract/result.json`. Runtime inputs, logs, exact rerun command, hashes and cleanup are retained there. Both owned local databases were stopped and removed. No real body was read/copied and no remote DDL/DML occurred.
+
+Source/spec patch from 5745197060: `review-from-5745197060-sparse-heatmaps.patch`. Generated immutable evidence is covered separately by the file manifest.
